@* App.razor — rendered server-side by Blazor Static SSR (via Razor's
   HtmlRenderer) inside an ICP canister. The Mono.Cecil-rewritten
   RenderTreeFrameArrayBuilder (Wasp.AspNetCore/Vendor/) lets the
   AppendElement/Text/Markup pattern work on wasm32-wasi. *@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Blazor SSR on ICP</title>
</head>
<body style="font-family: system-ui; max-width: 720px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem;">
    <h1 style="color: #2563eb;">Blazor SSR on ICP</h1>
    <p>This page is server-rendered by <strong>Blazor Static SSR</strong> (Razor's <code>HtmlRenderer</code>), inside a WebAssembly canister on the Internet Computer.</p>
    <p>Counter value: <strong style="font-size: 2rem; color: #16a34a;">@RazorOnIcCanister.GetCount()</strong></p>
    <form method="post" action="/counter/bump">
        <button type="submit" style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; font-size: 1rem; cursor: pointer;">Bump counter</button>
    </form>
    <hr />
    <small>
        Counter is persisted via <code>StableCell&lt;int&gt;</code> and survives canister upgrades.
        View source — there is no <code>_blazor.js</code>, no client-side WebAssembly hydration.
    </small>
</body>
</html>
